 "caption": "Up in the red sky of Edvard Munch's The Scream (1893) there's a faint line of pencil: \"Kan kun være malet af en gal Mand!\" — \"Can only have been painted by a madman!\"\n\nIt was first mentioned in 1904, when a Danish critic assumed a visitor had scribbled it. For years it was taken for graffiti.\n\nIn 2021, preparing the painting for its new building, Norway's National Museum photographed it in infrared and compared the writing with Munch's letters and diaries. Curator Mai Britt Guleng's verdict: the handwriting is without a doubt Munch's own.\n\nThe likely trigger: in 1895 Munch showed The Scream in Kristiania (now Oslo). At a student debate, the medical student Johan Scharffenberg said Munch's paintings, especially Self-Portrait with Cigarette, made him question the artist's sanity. The museum thinks Munch wrote the line soon after. The curator reads it as irony, but he was hurt, and kept returning to it in his notes for years.\n\n🖤 Irony, or a cry for help? What do you read in it?",
 "caption_short": "Someone wrote \"can only have been painted by a madman\" on The Scream. It was blamed on a vandal. In 2021, infrared showed it was Munch himself. 🖤",
 "youtube_title": "Who wrote \"madman\" on Munch's The Scream?",
